{"title":"Surge pricing is coming for your rent","link":"https://www.usermag.co/p/surge-pricing-is-coming-for-your","date":1753719122000,"content":"<div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg\" width=\"1365\" height=\"768\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ZvnO!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F83a71324-1112-4952-964f-6f9fd212a298_1365x768.jpeg 1456w\" /><div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>AI is about to make you pay more for everything. Surveillance pricing, where AI systems predict how much you’ll pay for something and raise prices accordingly, is being incorporated into every aspect of modern life, and soon even your rent. </p><div></div><p>RealPage, an AI platform, is <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250716862220/en/RealPage-Continues-to-Redefine-the-Resident-Experience-with-Acquisition-of-Livble-a-Leader-in-Flexible-Payment-Solutions\">acquiring</a> payments processor Livble, giving landlords the ability to subdivide monthly rents based on a tenants’ real-time cash flow data.</p><p>“RealPage is entering the surveillance pricing game. What could possibly go wrong?” Lee Hepner, an anti-monopoly law and policy expert at The American Economic Liberties Project <a href=\"https://x.com/LeeHepner/status/1949601950439297410\">posted to X</a>. </p><p>In a press release about the announcement, Josh Ehrlich, Co-founder and CEO, Livble said that “RealPage and Livble have a shared vision to redefine the rent payment experience.” By teaming up, the companies say that hope to “accelerate the adoption of flexible payment options at scale for both property managers and residents.”</p><p>While all of this sounds benign, as Hepner <a href=\"https://x.com/LeeHepner/status/1949623885231423583\">points out</a>, it certainly sounds like these \"flexible rent payments\" will likely not lead to “financial wellness for millions of renters\" Instead, this new AI-powered system will likely be used as a tool for property managers to access sensitive financial data, map individual demand curves, hike rents, and constructively evict tenets. </p><p>But rent is just the beginning. As Fast Company’s Chris Stokel-Walker recently wrote, AI is going to put dynamic pricing into everything you buy. The cost of everything from airline flights to your daily coffee to basic grocery items may soon be personalized based on a massive amount of harvested data and opaque AI systems. </p><p>“Firms are increasingly willing to squeeze consumers for every penny,” Kerry Tan, professor of economics at Loyola University Maryland <a href=\"https://archive.ph/LlYpP#selection-615.85-615.148\">told FastCo</a>. “That’s why companies like Disney can implement variable pricing for perks like Lightning Lane passes, or why Las Vegas casinos continue to raise resort fees.”</p><p>Ever since political leaders began to force people back to work amidst the ongoing pandemic back in 2021, the consumer environment has become more hostile. Political leaders have relentlessly prioritized the interests of business leaders and corporate profits over average working people. </p><p>Sporting events were first to institute dynamic pricing centered around demand for different team match ups. More recently, airlines have rolled out targeted pricing, where certain people are prompted to pay more for a plane ticket based on their geography and data available via their browser. </p><p>Supermarkets across Europe have <a href=\"https://www.retaildesignsolutions.com/the-future-of-retail-embracing-digital-pricing/\">also embraced AI-driven dynamic pricing</a>, with grocery retailers in Spain, Italy, Germany and the Netherlands using AI-powered systems that change the price of goods based on factors like sell-by dates, stock levels, and demand patterns. </p><p>Tim Quigley, a management professor at the University of Georgia, told Fast Company, “If [a company] knows there’s an ad and a bunch of people in a city searching for a piece of hardware at Best Buy, maybe the price goes up. It’s those sorts of things AI can do without human intervention.”</p><p>Hotels are another industry that may begin charging you more based on what you’re willing to pay. Any business that “can tap into that difference and charge you closer to what your willingness to pay is, they’re going to extract a lot more profits,” Quigley said, adding that the result would be “a miserable existence” for consumers. </p><p>As Stokel-Walker notes, <a href=\"https://archive.ph/LlYpP#selection-669.0-662.2\">the solution starts with protecting personal data</a>. “Companies are using this data in ways that you and I could have never imagined,” Quigley said. “Maybe we ought to put some basic protections in place to say the customer, the individual—[we] own our data.” </p><p><a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/surge-pricing-is-coming-for-your?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=share&amp;action=share&amp;token=eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMTMxMTk5NywicG9zdF9pZCI6MTY4OTU0Mzg0LCJpYXQiOjE3NTM3MzMzNzQsImV4cCI6MTc1NjMyNTM3NCwiaXNzIjoicHViLTMyMzgiLCJzdWIiOiJwb3N0LXJlYWN0aW9uIn0.X7jRJyVSE5p3bO3mDBvxBblwX3_CsRpcR_X1dAfVjX4\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h2>What I’m reading</h2><p><strong>He didn’t set out to create a kids’ company. Roblox’s “Builderman” wound up with one anyway.</strong> </p><p>Founder and CEO David Baszucki tells us the origin story and what’s next for a company that has nearly tripled in stock price and caught a lot of controversy over the past year. - <em><a href=\"https://sherwood.news/tech/he-didnt-set-out-to-create-a-kids-company-robloxs-builderman-wound-up-with/\">Sherwood</a></em></p><p><strong>Prosecutors used an AI tool to send a man to prison for life. Now the person who created it is under investigation.</strong></p><p>Adam Mosher claimed his AI tool Cybercheck helped cops and prosecutors with thousands of cases. Now he's under investigation for false testimony. - <em><a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/ai-crime-tool-cybercheck-founder-adam-mosher-investigation-2024-8\">Business Insider</a></em></p><p><strong>Are You a Canceled Celeb in Need of Great PR? Dial 1-900-Mitchell Jackson</strong></p><p>The former Vice staffer has built out a boutique business catering to the internet’s most notorious figures. “You’ll never starve in America if you’re shameless,” he tells VF. - <em><a href=\"https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/mitchell-jackson-vice-media-pr?utm_campaign=dhtwitter&amp;utm_content=%3Cmedia_url%3E&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_source=twitter\">Vanity Fair</a></em></p><p><strong>Sniffies Translates Cruising for the Digital Age</strong></p><p>Open it up, log on anonymously, and you’ll get a real-time sexual map of your neighborhood. - <em><a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/culture/annals-of-inquiry/sniffies-translates-cruising-for-the-digital-age\">The New Yorker</a></em></p><p><strong>YouTuber Tim Pool Wants Answers—and Trusts No One</strong></p><p>The right-wing streamer built an empire while stoking suspicion of the government and mainstream media. Will President Trump be his next target? - <em><a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/business/media/podcaster-tim-pool-wants-answersand-trusts-no-one-a430ab06\">The Wall Street Journal</a></em></p><p><strong>An American mega-influencer flew to Lithuania. Then the chaos began.</strong></p><p>The streamer IShowSpeed drank pink soup in the Baltics and marveled at cars in China. Are his tours propaganda, or just good advertising? - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/2025.07.27-113131/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/07/27/ishowspeed-streamer-darren-watkins-lithuania/\">Washington Post</a></em></p><p><strong>Crypto kidnapping: How armed gangs are hunting the internet's high rollers</strong></p><p>Kidnapping and extortion are growing concerns in the crypto world, with cases rising alongside the price of bitcoin. - <em><a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/rcna215047\">NBC News</a></em></p><p><a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/surge-pricing-is-coming-for-your?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=share&amp;action=share&amp;token=eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMTMxMTk5NywicG9zdF9pZCI6MTY4OTU0Mzg0LCJpYXQiOjE3NTM3MzMzNzQsImV4cCI6MTc1NjMyNTM3NCwiaXNzIjoicHViLTMyMzgiLCJzdWIiOiJwb3N0LXJlYWN0aW9uIn0.X7jRJyVSE5p3bO3mDBvxBblwX3_CsRpcR_X1dAfVjX4\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h2>User Mag news rundown</h2><ul><li><p>Ghosting is out, <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/lifestyle/relationships/dating-ghosting-breakup-text-3415d5fb\">speed dumping is in</a>. </p></li><li><p>Democratic candidates are <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/07/26/politics/democrats-weightlifting-videos\">posting weightlifting videos</a> hoping that it will help them win the midterms.</p></li><li><p>You can now <a href=\"https://nypost.com/2025/07/25/business/venmo-paypal-users-can-help-us-government-pay-down-36-7t-debt/\">Venmo the United States</a> to help pay off the national debt.</p></li><li><p>Netflix is <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/netflix-seeking-podcast-head-chasing-new-cheaper-content-forms-2025-7\">searching for a video podcasting head</a>.</p></li><li><p>North Korean scammers <a href=\"https://archive.ph/U7xYd#selection-725.0-730.0\">are obsessed with Minions</a>. </p><ul><li><p>References to Minions are so ubiquitous among North Korean hackers that investigators pursuing suspects view Despicable Me references as a sign they’re on the right track.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>The <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/tea-app-data-breach-leak-4chan-c95d5bb2cabe9d1b8ec0ca8903503b29\">Tea app</a> was intended to help women date safely. <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/tea-app-data-breach-leak-4chan-c95d5bb2cabe9d1b8ec0ca8903503b29\">Then it got hacked</a>.</p></li><li><p>Fictional idol bands from Netflix’s ‘Kpop Demon Hunters’ <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/arts-culture/music/kpop-demon-hunters-netflix-spotify-91566609\">have achieved unprecedented popularity in the U.S.</a></p></li><li><p>A European chip brand made tortilla chips that <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/713693/9-volt-battery-tortilla-chips-rewind-taste-test\">taste like licking a battery.</a></p></li><li><p>A woman was <a href=\"https://www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/i-fell-love-ai-bot-35626957\">ghosted by her AI boyfriend</a>. </p></li><li><p>Gentle parenting is out and FAFO parenting is in as parents try to <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/lifestyle/fafo-gentle-parenting-625da658\">“out feral” their kids feral</a>. </p></li><li><p>A survey of <a href=\"https://on.substack.com/p/the-substack-ai-report\">2,000 Substack publishers found</a> that 45% use AI, and 85% of tech publications use it. (Not <em>User Mag</em> though!!!!!!!!!) </p></li><li><p>An AI therapist went haywire and <a href=\"https://futurism.com/ai-therapist-haywire-mental-health\">urged user to go on a killing spree</a>.</p></li><li><p>Democrats get the <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/democratic-party-poll-voter-confidence-july-2025-9db38021\">lowest rating from voters in 35 years</a>. </p></li><li><p>Scientists <a href=\"https://archive.ph/7R6t8#selection-1583.0-1587.83\">bust the myth</a> that 10,000 steps are required for good health. (7,000 is more than fine). </p></li><li><p>Elon Musk is now officially worth $405.6 billion, projected to become <a href=\"https://x.com/GlobeEyeNews/status/1949503125976731927\">the world’s first trillionaire by 2027</a>.</p></li><li><p>Vogue Australia ran ads for Guess clothing <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgeqe084nn4o\">featuring AI generated models</a>.</p></li><li><p>A baby girl grew a micropenis from lying <a href=\"https://www.vice.com/en/article/baby-girl-grew-a-micropenis-from-lying-on-her-dads-chest/\">on her dad’s chest while</a> he was using testosterone gel.</p></li><li><p>Waves are a new brand of <a href=\"https://petapixel.com/2025/07/24/waves-are-dumb-camera-glasses-aimed-at-creators/\">“all-day” camera glasses</a> designed for content creators.</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/e-news-canceled-1236328449/\">E! News has been cancelled</a> after 34 years on air.   </p></li><li><p>More people are <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/lifestyle/dry-wedding-alcohol-relationships-6d2452db\">having dry weddings</a>. </p></li><li><p>DOGE has an AI tool to help decide <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/doge-ai-federal-de-regulation-tool-leaked\">which federal regulations to delete</a>. The tool has misread the language of the law multiple times already.</p></li><li><p>The rightwing media is <a href=\"https://archive.is/rnGGq#selection-1585.0-1585.51\">stoking culture wars</a> in Germany.</p></li><li><p>Half of wealth concentration in the U.S. over the past dozen years <a href=\"https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/political-commentary/america-oligarchy-billionaires-sanders-trump-musk-data-1235393910/\">has benefited just 19 families</a>.</p></li><li><p>AI tools like ChatGPT are <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/its-most-empathetic-voice-my-life-how-ai-is-transforming-lives-neurodivergent-2025-07-26/\">helping neurodivergent people communicate</a> more clearly and confidently.</p></li><li><p> Google is testing <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/25/google-is-testing-a-vibe-coding-app-called-opal/\">a vibe-coding app called Opal</a>.</p></li><li><p>A viral TikToker with over 1.6 million followers is <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/tiktok/tiktoker-heston-james-faces-9-years-in-jail-after-viral-prank-spree-3230655/\">facing 9 years in jail</a> after a months-long prank spree on local businesses. </p></li><li><p>Trump is vowing to “<a href=\"https://archive.ph/2y5ZS\">remove woke</a>” from AI.</p></li><li><p>Hundreds of trans Americans are <a href=\"https://archive.is/xKsiA#selection-261.31-261.97\">seeking refuge from Trump</a> in Canada.</p></li><li><p>Tesla <a href=\"https://futurism.com/tesla-most-hated\">is now the most</a> hated electric vehicle maker.</p></li><li><p>The U.S. birth rate just <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-birth-rate-all-time-low-cdc-data\">hit an all-time low</a>.</p></li><li><p> YouTube is set to make $40 billion dollars in ad revenue for 2025 <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/youtube/youtube-makes-creating-ai-videos-easier-as-platform-closes-in-on-40b-in-ad-revenue-3230438/\">due to a surge in AI generated Shorts.</a> Now they're introducing even more AI tools to make creating AI content easier. </p></li><li><p>Elon Musk says <a href=\"https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1948358524935004201\">he’s bringing back Vine</a> but “in AI form” whatever that means.</p></li><li><p> An Indian film company used AI to change the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/27/indian-film-company-to-re-release-romantic-drama-with-ai-happy-ending-raanjhaana-ambikapathy\">ending of a 2013 movie</a> without the director’s consent.</p></li><li><p>MrBeast is <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/youtube/mrbeast-is-making-a-big-budget-2d-animated-cartoon-series-starring-himself-3230871/\">making a 2D animated cartoon series</a> based on his toy line.</p></li><li><p>Facebook <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/713976/online-harassment-meta-social-media-environmental-activists\">ranks worst for online harassment</a>, according to a global survey.</p></li><li><p>The Internet Archive is now an <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/714058/the-internet-archive-is-now-an-official-hub-for-government-documents\">official hub for government documents</a>.</p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/surge-pricing-is-coming-for-your?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=share&amp;action=share&amp;token=eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMTMxMTk5NywicG9zdF9pZCI6MTY4OTU0Mzg0LCJpYXQiOjE3NTM3MzMzNzQsImV4cCI6MTc1NjMyNTM3NCwiaXNzIjoicHViLTMyMzgiLCJzdWIiOiJwb3N0LXJlYWN0aW9uIn0.X7jRJyVSE5p3bO3mDBvxBblwX3_CsRpcR_X1dAfVjX4\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h2>Good posts</h2><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!NFvw!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3713f7a8-3aea-40d4-a138-0020b827711c_944x704.png\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!NFvw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3713f7a8-3aea-40d4-a138-0020b827711c_944x704.png\" width=\"471\" height=\"351.2542372881356\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!NFvw!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3713f7a8-3aea-40d4-a138-0020b827711c_944x704.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!NFvw!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,